# Known bugs of the guide scripts, found by tools/check-vm-guest (Level 3) and waiting for Phase 1.
# Same columns and rules as scripts/fixtures/containers/known-issues:
#   id | pattern | what is wrong | OS majors (optional: "10" or "8,9"; empty means all) | package the system needs (optional)
# The pattern is an awk regular expression, matched against a leftover line such as
# "M /etc/fstab", "unit crond.service enabled", "boot entry missing vmlinuz-5.14.0 console=tty0",
# "nic missing eth1 channels Combined: 4" or "verify FAIL <text>". A dash means that the check
# finds the bug in code. A bug that is observed and not listed fails the run. So does a listed
# bug that is no longer observed on an image it applies to: delete its line in the change that
# fixes it.
no-rollback-02	^. /etc/(sysctl\.d/91-lowlat-rt\.conf|systemd/system\.conf)|irqbalance	02-cpu-isolation has no --rollback: it prints its usage and changes nothing
no-rollback-04	^nic 	04-network has no --rollback: NIC settings stay as applied until the next boot
no-rollback-07	limits\.d/90-lowlat|/etc/tuned/|^M /etc/fstab$|^boot entry extra .* (skew_tick=1|tsc=reliable|rcupdate\.rcu_normal_after_boot=1)$|(crond|rpcbind|nfs-client|remote-fs-pre|plymouth|auth-rpcgss|rpc_pipefs|rpc-statd|sysstat|pcscd|cpupower)	07-os-hygiene has no --rollback: limits, noatime in /etc/fstab, the tuned profile and state (on RHEL 8 its $tuned_params kernel arguments too), and the services it disabled stay
grub-cfg-left-regenerated	^M /(boot/grub2/grub\.cfg|etc/grub2(-efi)?\.cfg)$	01-grub-bootloader --apply regenerates grub.cfg with grub2-mkconfig, and --rollback leaves the regenerated file (with BLS entries the arguments are not in it, so the next boot is the same)
runtime-unit-left-enabled	lowlat-runtime\.service	apply-all has no --rollback: lowlat-runtime.service stays installed and enabled
virtio-irq-false-pass	-	verify-tuning passes the IRQ line of a virtio NIC that no guide placed
rhel10-no-system-conf	-	02-cpu-isolation --apply fails on RHEL 10: /etc/systemd/system.conf does not exist there (the file is in /usr/lib/systemd)	10
tuned-profile-dir-rhel10	-	07-os-hygiene writes the low-latency profile to /etc/tuned/low-latency, but tuned on RHEL 10 reads /etc/tuned/profiles: tuned-adm rejects it and apply-all stops	10	tuned
rhel8-rollback-args-return	^running cmdline extra 	on RHEL 8 the kernel arguments that 01 added are back on /proc/cmdline after its rollback and a reboot: grubby cleans kernelopts in grubenv and /etc/default/grub, yet the kernel boots with the same arguments as the fallback kernelopts that the apply-time grub2-mkconfig wrote into grub.cfg (the grub evidence of tools/check-vm shows it; the cause is for Phase 1)	8
coalesce-unsupported-verify-fails	^verify FAIL .*rx-usecs=0$	04-network asks for rx-usecs=0 on the critical NIC, and verify-tuning fails when the driver has no interrupt coalescing (virtio-net on the RHEL 8 kernel)	8
